<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <meta name="description" content="Differential expression analysis report generated by RNA-seq Explorer">
    <title>{{ config.output.report_title }}</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #333; max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem; }
        h1, h2, h3 { color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee; padding-bottom: 0.3em; }
        .alert { padding: 1rem; margin: 1rem 0; border-radius: 4px; background-color: #f8d7da; color: #721c24; border: 1px solid #f5c6cb; }
        .metadata { background: #f8f9fa; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid #e9ecef; }
        .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
        .img-container { text-align: center; border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 6px; background: #fff; }
        .img-container img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
        .stats { display: flex; gap: 2rem; margin: 2rem 0; }
        .stat-box { background: #e3f2fd; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 6px; text-align: center; flex: 1; border: 1px solid #bbdefb; }
        .stat-value { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: bold; color: #1976d2; }
        table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 1rem; }
        th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px; text-align: left; }
        th { background-color: #f2f2f2; }
        .observation { background-color: #e2e3e5; color: #383d41; border: 1px solid #d6d8db; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; margin: 1rem 0; font-style: italic; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>{{ config.output.report_title }}</h1>
    
    <div class="metadata">
        <h2>Analysis Metadata</h2>
        <table>
            {% set cond_col = contrast_spec.condition_column if contrast_spec else config.design.condition_column %}
            {% set ref_level = contrast_spec.reference_level if contrast_spec else config.design.reference_level %}
            {% set comp_level = contrast_spec.comparison_level if contrast_spec else config.design.comparison_level %}
            
            {% if contrast_spec %}
            <tr><th>Contrast Name</th><td>{{ contrast_spec.name }}</td></tr>
            {% endif %}
            <tr><th>Condition Column</th><td>{{ cond_col }}</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Reference Level</th><td>{{ ref_level }}</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Comparison Level</th><td>{{ comp_level }}</td></tr>
            {% if config.design.paired_or_block_column %}
            <tr><th>Blocking Covariate</th><td>{{ config.design.paired_or_block_column }}</td></tr>
            {% endif %}
            <tr><th>FDR Threshold</th><td>{{ config.thresholds.fdr }}</td></tr>
            <tr><th>|Log2FC| Threshold</th><td>{{ config.thresholds.absolute_log2_fold_change }}</td></tr>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="metadata">
        <h2>Data Provenance</h2>
        <table>
            <tr><th>Counts File</th><td><code>{{ config.input.counts }}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><th>Counts SHA-256</th><td><code>{{ manifest.counts_sha256 }}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><th>Metadata File</th><td><code>{{ config.input.metadata }}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><th>Metadata SHA-256</th><td><code>{{ manifest.metadata_sha256 }}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><th>Config SHA-256</th><td><code>{{ manifest.config_sha256 }}</code></td></tr>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat-box">
            <div class="stat-value">{{ total_genes }}</div>
            <div>Total Genes Tested</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-box">
            <div class="stat-value">{{ sig_up }}</div>
            <div>Significantly Upregulated</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-box">
            <div class="stat-value">{{ sig_down }}</div>
            <div>Significantly Downregulated</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2>QC Observations</h2>
    <div class="metadata" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        <h3>Pre-filtering Summary</h3>
        <p>
            <strong>Genes before filtering:</strong> {{ filtering.genes_before }}<br>
            <strong>Genes after filtering:</strong> {{ filtering.genes_after }}<br>
            <strong>Genes removed:</strong> {{ filtering.genes_before - filtering.genes_after }}<br>
            <strong>Rule:</strong> kept genes with &ge; {{ filtering.min_count }} counts in &ge; {{ filtering.min_samples }} samples
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="observation">
        <strong>Observation:</strong> The PCA and Sample Distance heatmaps below visualize sample clustering based on overall expression profiles. Clustering associated with the condition variable indicates systematic transcriptional differences between groups. <em>This is an observational assessment of data structure, not a causal conclusion.</em>
    </div>

    <div class="img-container" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; justify-content: space-around; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 300px; margin: 10px;">
            <h3>Library Sizes</h3>
            <img src="library_sizes.png" alt="{{ plot_alts.library_sizes if (plot_alts and plot_alts.library_sizes) else 'Library sizes per sample bar chart' }}">
            <p><small>Total number of reads assigned to genes per sample.</small></p>
        </div>
        <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 300px; margin: 10px;">
            <h3>Principal Component Analysis</h3>
            <img src="pca.png" alt="{{ plot_alts.pca if (plot_alts and plot_alts.pca) else 'Principal component analysis scatter plot of normalized counts' }}">
            <p><small>PCA on log1p-transformed normalized counts.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="img-container" style="max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; margin-top: 1rem;">
        <h3>Sample Distances</h3>
        <img src="sample_distances.png" alt="{{ plot_alts.sample_distances if (plot_alts and plot_alts.sample_distances) else 'Sample distance matrix heatmap' }}">
        <p><small>Euclidean distance matrix on log1p-transformed normalized counts.</small></p>
    </div>

    <h2>Methodology</h2>
    <div class="metadata">
        <p>This pipeline employs standard statistical methodologies for bulk RNA-seq differential expression analysis. It does not introduce novel mathematical approaches.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Model:</strong> Generalized Linear Model (GLM) assuming a negative binomial distribution for gene counts.</li>
            <li><strong>Normalization:</strong> Median-of-ratios method to compute sample-specific size factors, accounting for library size and RNA composition differences.</li>
            <li><strong>Statistical Test:</strong> Wald test for significance of coefficients in the GLM.</li>
            <li><strong>Multiple Testing Correction:</strong> Benjamini-Hochberg procedure to control the False Discovery Rate (FDR).</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Citations:</strong> Core statistical computations are performed via <a href="https://github.com/owkin/PyDESeq2">PyDESeq2</a>, a Python implementation of the <a href="https://genomebiology.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s13059-014-0550-8">DESeq2</a> algorithm (Love, Huber, and Anders 2014).</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Differential Expression Results</h2>
    <div class="alert" style="background-color: #fff3cd; color: #856404; border-color: #ffeeba;">
        <strong>Threshold Interpretation:</strong> FDR and fold-change thresholds are conventional cutoffs, not biological truths. A gene failing these thresholds may still be biologically relevant, and a gene passing them requires independent validation.
    </div>
    
    <div class="img-container" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; justify-content: space-around; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 300px; margin: 10px;">
            <h3>Volcano Plot</h3>
            <img src="volcano.png" alt="{{ plot_alts.volcano if (plot_alts and plot_alts.volcano) else 'Volcano plot of differential expression results' }}">
            <p><small>Genes passing both FDR and Fold Change thresholds are highlighted.</small></p>
        </div>
        <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 300px; margin: 10px;">
            <h3>MA Plot</h3>
            <img src="ma_plot.png" alt="{{ plot_alts.ma if (plot_alts and plot_alts.ma) else 'MA plot of differential expression results' }}">
            <p><small>Relationship between mean normalized count and fold change.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="img-container" style="max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; margin-top: 1rem;">
        <h3>Top DE Genes Heatmap</h3>
        <img src="top_genes_heatmap.png" alt="{{ plot_alts.top_genes_heatmap if (plot_alts and plot_alts.top_genes_heatmap) else 'Top differentially expressed genes clustered heatmap' }}">
        <p><small>Expression patterns of the most statistically significant genes. Z-scoring highlights relative differences across samples.</small></p>
    </div>

    {% if top_genes %}
    <h2>Gene Annotations (Top 50 DE Genes)</h2>
    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
        <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Gene ID</th>
                    {% if top_genes[0].gene_symbol is defined %}<th>Symbol</th>{% endif %}
                    <th>Log2FC</th>
                    <th>padj</th>
                    {% if top_genes[0].description is defined %}<th>Description</th>{% endif %}
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for row in top_genes %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ row.gene_id }}</td>
                    {% if row.gene_symbol is defined %}<td>{{ row.gene_symbol }}</td>{% endif %}
                    <td>{{ "%.2f"|format(row.log2FoldChange) }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.2e"|format(row.padj) }}</td>
                    {% if row.description is defined %}<td>{{ row.description }}</td>{% endif %}
                </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if enrichment %}
    <h2>Pathway Enrichment (Exploratory)</h2>
    <div class="alert" style="background-color: #e2e3e5; color: #383d41; border-color: #d6d8db;">
        <strong>EXPLORATORY ONLY:</strong> Enrichment results are derived from database annotations and statistical tests on gene lists. They do not constitute biological validation.
    </div>
    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
        <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Term</th>
                    <th>Overlap</th>
                    <th>P-value</th>
                    <th>Adjusted P-value</th>
                    <th>Genes</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for row in enrichment %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ row.Term }}</td>
                    <td>{{ row.Overlap }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.2e"|format(row['P-value']) }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.2e"|format(row['Adjusted P-value']) }}</td>
                    <td><small>{{ row.Genes }}</small></td>
                </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if config.dataset_limitations %}
    <h2>Dataset-Specific Limitations</h2>
    <div class="alert" style="background-color: #fff3cd; color: #856404; border-color: #ffeeba;">
        <ul style="margin-bottom: 0;">
            {% for limitation in config.dataset_limitations %}
            <li>{{ limitation }}</li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    <h2>General Limitations</h2>
    <div class="alert">
        <strong>LIMITATION NOTICE:</strong> RNA-seq Explorer is a reproducible, configuration-driven toolkit for exploratory, non-clinical bulk RNA-seq analysis.
        <ul style="margin-top: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
            <li><strong>No Causal Claims:</strong> Differential expression does not establish causality. The results are strictly for hypothesis generation.</li>
            <li><strong>Sample Size Constraints:</strong> Bulk RNA-seq experiments often lack sufficient statistical power. Results must be interpreted carefully and require independent experimental validation.</li>
            <li><strong>Count-Based Assumptions:</strong> This pipeline analyzes raw gene-level counts and cannot detect isoform-level dynamics or allele-specific expression.</li>
            <li><strong>Not for Clinical Use:</strong> Must not be used for clinical, diagnostic, or biomarker-validated conclusions.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="metadata">
        <h2>How to Reproduce</h2>
        <p>To perfectly reproduce this analysis environment and report, run the following exact command from the project root:</p>
        <pre style="background: #eee; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>{{ manifest.command }}</code></pre>
        
        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Reproducibility Manifest</h3>
        <p>The following environment details were captured at runtime:</p>
        <table>
            <tr><th>RNA-seq Explorer Version</th><td>{{ manifest.rnax_version }}</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Python Version</th><td>{{ manifest.python_version }}</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Platform</th><td>{{ manifest.platform }}</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Git Commit</th><td>{{ manifest.git_commit or "Not in a git repository" }}</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Timestamp (UTC)</th><td>{{ manifest.timestamp }}</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Random Seed</th><td>{{ manifest.random_seed }}</td></tr>
            <tr>
                <th>Package Versions</th>
                <td>
                    <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem;">
                    {% for pkg, ver in manifest.packages.items() %}
                        <li>{{ pkg }}: {{ ver }}</li>
                    {% endfor %}
                    </ul>
                </td>
            </tr>
        </table>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
